Thus, from bare reading of Article 13(2) of the Constitution of India, it is clear that the State cannot make laws that:
(i) Take away or abridge the rights conferred by Part III of the Constitution;
(ii) Contravene this clause Meaning thereby, the Constitution of India safeguards the citizens of India and the State must adhere to the cardinal principles of natural justice before enacting any law.
